  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking bug** in `share-editing`:\n\n**[P1] View-only shares can edit unlocked documents — `src/guard.js:12`**\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` is parsed as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, so it checks the READ bit (`1`), not WRITE (`4`).\n\nConfirmed:\n- `{ mask: READ, locked: false }` → `canEdit` returns **true**.\n- `{ mask: WRITE, locked: false }` → returns **0**, incorrectly denying editing.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`, or parenthesize the bitwise expression. Add regression tests for a read-only share and a WRITE-only share; the current editor test masks the bug because editors have both bits.\n\nAll **6 existing tests pass**. I also checked the toggle behavior across all 16 masks; no issues there. No code changed.",
